\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Trust contract}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}
\tag{provenance}

\p{A \strong{trust contract} #{\operatorname{Trust}(P)} is a predicate on a
post-training protocol and its recorded execution. It requires evaluation
independence, policy and data provenance, declared information access, and
complete lifecycle-cost accounting.}

\p{This is an FTIP proposal. Its clauses are motivated by standard held-out
evaluation and by concrete provenance failures in replay or trajectory studies.
For example, a future checkpoint cannot be used to train a path predictor and
then counted as information available at an earlier step.}

\p{The contract is not a proof that a benchmark measures intelligence. It is a
minimum admissibility gate. Each experiment must instantiate the predicate as
auditable conditions.}
